cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use plantcv-mcp in your work, please cite it as below. PlantCV is the
  analysis library this server wraps and must be cited separately — see
  references.
title: plantcv-mcp
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server exposing PlantCV as a measurement
  instrument: it returns plant trait numbers together with the segmentation
  overlay they were computed from, and refuses to return numbers when the
  segmentation is degenerate. Mask validity is two-sided, so an inverted
  threshold — which otherwise reports the background as the plant with no error
  at all — is an outcome the system can express as a failure. Traits convert to
  real-world units from an explicit table rather than from PlantCV's unit
  strings, and batch analysis withholds traits for any image that trips a
  blocking guard instead of reporting an unreviewed number.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arnold
    given-names: Jaret
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4055-5238"
repository-code: "https://github.com/musharna/plantcv-mcp"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21713516
url: "https://pypi.org/project/plantcv-mcp/"
license: MIT
version: 1.4.0
date-released: "2026-08-29"
keywords:
  - plantcv
  - phenotyping
  - plant-science
  - image-analysis
  - computer-vision
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp
references:
  - type: article
    title: "PlantCV v4: Image analysis software for high-throughput plant phenotyping"
    authors:
      - name: "The PlantCV development team"
    journal: The Plant Phenome Journal
    volume: 9
    issue: 1
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1002/ppj2.70065
    notes: >-
      The analysis library this server wraps, pinned at plantcv==4.11.3 — so the
      v4 paper is the correct citation, not the widely-cited v2 paper (Gehan et
      al. 2017, 10.7717/peerj.4088). Cite PlantCV for any published result
      produced with this tool; citing the wrapper does not discharge that. The
      byline runs to 62 authors and is deliberately not transcribed here: resolve
      the DOI for the authoritative list rather than trusting a hand-copied one.
